,"date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:41:17-07:00","id":298179,"title":"","content":"I contracted that disease from Neuroshima RPG that makes your skin pale and react allergic to sunlight (and burning without taking drugs).<br /> <br /> I had trouble explaining everyone I'm not a vampire and was chased around by misguided Hunters and people of local Prince for being unsanctioned<br /> <br /> It was like being a reverse Nicholas Cage<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not a vampire!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T13:44:36-07:00","id":298395,"title":"","content":"So, I had some interesting dreams last night. I may have to ask Papa Bear to do some dream interpretation here.<br /> <br /> 1. I was in an awesome minis shop that displayed all sorts of fantastic Gunpla style model kits and Warhammer type miniatures, eliciting a &quot;kid in a candy/toy store&quot; feeling. There was some amazingly cool stuff in there that I'm not sure could have existed in real life, but whenever I tried to touch something to get a closer look, I would inevitably break something fragile and have to hurriedly fix it. I had some mixed emotions by the end of that one.<br /> <br /> 2. This one was more in depth: It was sometime during the Cold War, and the Mainland U.S. was being invaded by the Soviet Union. I wasn't sure exactly when during the Cold War this was taking place, as we seemed to have some modern technology (like flatscreens), but the military tech and gear had a very definite post-WWII-Vietnam-war vibe. It seemed that the majority of the fighting was taking place on rivers and canals that criss-crossed America, and the primary weapons for the fight were hovertanks that floated across the waterways. They didn't appear to be very practical though; the tanks were a bit bigger than regular tanks, and the cupolas were not armored: the crew members were exposed, but that didn't seem to worry them.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the dream didn't cover any of the actual fighting, because that would just be too <i>interesting</i> (sigh). Instead, it followed two principal characters, both fictional: the first was the President of the United States, who was trying to win the conflict or resolve the situation peacefully while navigating the perilous waters of politics and espionage. The second was the XO of one of the hovertanks, who was trying to usurp command by exploiting the fact that the existing CO was erroneously declared KIA during one of the more chaotic battles.<br /> <br /> One thing that struck me after I had woken up was that, as far as I can remember, there were no female characters in any of the dreams I had. They may or may not have been in the background, but neither I nor the dream focus characters interacted with any for the duration. This seems rather odd and a bit distressing to me; the only reason I can think of for there being no women in the stories was because the dreams did not have a romantic or sexual element, a thought that just raises further questions.<br /> <br /> So yeah, odd. Anybody have any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 10-31-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:37:07-08:00","id":299876,"title":"","content":"I should maybe take a little break from Changeling. I get dreams like being abducted by aliens vulnerable to iron, escaping soon enough with more changed captives to get &quot;only&quot; permamently ensorcelled and then hanging out with my new peculiar friends because sure why not and surely that &quot;Spring Court&quot; they talk about has some fine shit, which end ups with me being stoned and banging all those kemonomimi Changeling girls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:12:48-08:00","id":301181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=298395#post298395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I had some interesting dreams last night. I may have to ask Papa Bear to do some dream interpretation here.<br /> <br /> 1. I was in an awesome minis shop that displayed all sorts of fantastic Gunpla style model kits and Warhammer type miniatures, eliciting a &quot;kid in a candy/toy store&quot; feeling. There was some amazingly cool stuff in there that I'm not sure could have existed in real life, but whenever I tried to touch something to get a closer look, I would inevitably break something fragile and have to hurriedly fix it. I had some mixed emotions by the end of that one.<br /> <br /> 2. This one was more in depth: It was sometime during the Cold War, and the Mainland U.S. was being invaded by the Soviet Union. I wasn't sure exactly when during the Cold War this was taking place, as we seemed to have some modern technology (like flatscreens), but the military tech and gear had a very definite post-WWII-Vietnam-war vibe. It seemed that the majority of the fighting was taking place on rivers and canals that criss-crossed America, and the primary weapons for the fight were hovertanks that floated across the waterways. They didn't appear to be very practical though; the tanks were a bit bigger than regular tanks, and the cupolas were not armored: the crew members were exposed, but that didn't seem to worry them.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the dream didn't cover any of the actual fighting, because that would just be too <i>interesting</i> (sigh). Instead, it followed two principal characters, both fictional: the first was the President of the United States, who was trying to win the conflict or resolve the situation peacefully while navigating the perilous waters of politics and espionage. The second was the XO of one of the hovertanks, who was trying to usurp command by exploiting the fact that the existing CO was erroneously declared KIA during one of the more chaotic battles.<br /> <br /> One thing that struck me after I had woken up was that, as far as I can remember, there were no female characters in any of the dreams I had. They may or may not have been in the background, but neither I nor the dream focus characters interacted with any for the duration. This seems rather odd and a bit distressing to me; the only reason I can think of for there being no women in the stories was because the dreams did not have a romantic or sexual element, a thought that just raises further questions.<br /> <br /> So yeah, odd. Anybody have any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I know a bit more about Jim's personal life, so I was about to tailor his more. I'll have to keep it a little more vague for you.<br /> <br /> 1) Might be nothing more than the usual &quot;I wish&quot; kind of dream. The breaking and fixing could symbolize that you don't feel like they should exist at all, so you tear them down and build them back up again your own way. Could also mean that you don't feel like you would belong in such a place on a superficial level (the breaking of them), but deep down you know your worth (rebuilding them). Could also be some jealousy there, which is why you break them and remake them yourself.<br /> <br /> 2) Well, the internal struggle is obvious, but there's a lot of reasons that can cause an internal struggle. The fact that you specifically remembered that there were no women throws out the other obvious conclusion, you like men. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But it could also symbolize the struggle to GET someone in your life (if there isn't anyone) and you're trying to decide if you need to take the approach of getting someone new (Prez getting solution thru difficult navigation) or going back to someone you've had in your life previously (XO looking to take over CO). OR it could be over an internal struggle and the reasons are unknown to me because I don't know you well enough and you'll have to figure it out yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:48:16-08:00","id":301386,"title":"","content":"Reasonable interpretations. I see some things that make sense on reflection, others I know for a fact to be untrue (I'll leave you to guess which one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> Thank you, Ursine Paternal figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-promethe