k up again. The little girl obviously had no expression to be seen as it turned like a drunken marionette to face its family, but nevertheless they were sure her lips were split in a wide, hateful, insane grin that matched that on their son's face. As he crawled out from the shadows, the meat had been flensed from his bones from the shoulders down. The meat of his neck sagged and flapped loosely, since it was only anchored from above now.<br /> I wish I could say my outrage was caused by the deaths of two innocent children, but it wasn't. It was offense that this abomination should have the temerity to exist without my permission, to manifest itself in front of me in defiance of my will. I would kill it for offending me, so I hurled myself at the children who I now knew were not just dead but were part of it forever and ever, a fact which only made me angrier. One hand seized the girl by the crown of the head and I whipped her body over my shoulder, shattering the vertebrae in her neck like a farmer who doesn't want to get blood on his ax killing a chicken; the boy I felt my claws wanting to extend for and I fought the impulse down. I would kill him in my human form, with my fists. My rage was intoxicating but I wouldn't let it take my humanity; I was already too close to the edge. I could hear myself roaring and I sounded like a gorilla, not a man. I grasped the bones and rent them, pulling them apart until no force could reanimate them.<br /> Behind me, the parents were screaming, because the abomination didn't need the childrens' bodies to attack them. The father already felt its fingers on his neck, and I charged at them, ready to grasp the thing and beat it to death, but even as I did I knew I was helpless. I was insane with rage at the point, and my heart was so full of hate I had no capacity to feel the fear I needed to feel in order for it to become real to me; and if it wasn't real to me, I could not put my fists on it.<br /> I woke up before the dream showed me what happened to the parents, but I assume it was nothing good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was waiting for you to shift into Gauru form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:32:23-07:00","id":674592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=674500#post674500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Would you like a hug? It sounds like you need one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was very impressed with that dream. My dreams are usually nothing but disconnected shit happening for no reason; this one was highly structured, carefully detailed, and the answer to almost every question but one (&quot;If I can't perceive the monster's reality, then how am I aware of the rules of its existence?&quot;) are at least heavily hinted at. It sounds like a nightmare, but like I said, I had no room for fear, just rage for the thing I wanted to kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=674548#post674548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was waiting for you to shift into Gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fuckin' know, right? I am pretty sure I was not a werewolf, though. I'm pretty sure I was some kind of reptilian shapeshifter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:57:03-07:00","id":674601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=674592#post674592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fuckin' know, right? I am pretty sure I was not a werewolf, though. I'm pretty sure I was some kind of reptilian shapeshifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archid form, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:02:23-07:00","id":674757,"title":"","content":"That's a Mokole thing, right? I never got into the Changing Breeds. I should. I imagine the .pdfs are fairly cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T21:44:57-07:00","id":674927,"title":"","content":"YES!! The.pdfs are rather affordable, and CB20 is really worth it if you want to maybe run or just see a multi-breed story in different ways than maybe the older stuff would inspire. They're all good, but some Breedbooks are just lively reads all on their own. Personal top 5 favorites just for reading the fluff and interesting crunch for a grin: Ratkin, Corax, Mokole, Nuwisha and Ananasi. <br /> <br /> The breeds add so much to Apocalypse that I honestly can't imagine the game universe without them.<br /> <br /> The same can I gess be said about Forsaken, but I'm not huge on Forsaken in the first place. It's not even a preference thing, I just haven't gotten the chance to play forsaken. If anyone would run it for me, I'd try it. Nobody runs games that I can attend. <br /> <br /> \u200bBack to dreams:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=674592#post674592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I was very impressed with that dream. My dreams are usually nothing but disconnected shit happening for no reason; this one was highly structured, carefully detailed, and the answer to almost every question but one (&quot;If I can't perceive the monster's reality, then how am I aware of the rules of its existence?&quot;) are at least heavily hinted at. It sounds like a nightmare, but like I said, I had no room for fear, just rage for the thing I wanted to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just described the two basic types of dreams I have:<br /> <br /> The disconnected shit dream where nothing makes sense. I'm usually wandering lost without any kind of reference point in these, sometimes even myself. Always just a random mess of things and feelings and half ideas that are gibberish in the morning.<br /> <br /> And the Pseudonightmare. Where EVERYTHING is clearly a fucking horror movie, but you might not be scared. Sad? Maybe. Angry to the point of being non-verbal? PROBABLY. A homicidal person or monster yourself? Often. <br /> <br /> Sometimes they're more subtle in intensity, but my dreamland is always a horror movie universe, if my dream makes any sense. I don't know why. It's always been that way. I once read something about the serial killer, Edmund Kemper. He called his inner world/thoughts his &quot;Vicious World&quot;. I can imagine that almost like an Umbral realm. Like Battleground if it lost its mind to the Wyrm. It's close to how I see my dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:25:11-07:00","id":686602,"title":"","content":"The last few nights i've had some bizzare as fuck dreams, I've always had vivid dreams but these pretty much won on the most clear i've ever had. I dont recall now what they were about except they left me sad so sad that when i wake from them i curl up with my baby girl and lay awake trying to make that pain in my gut go away.<br /> <br /> I saw my guide again in my dreams last night, no words were spoken just a quiet solem nod and a gesture for me to follow him. We ended up in a place i retreat to in my mind often, a calm clear overgrown clearing in a forest, a single small crystal clear waterfall with a shallow pool that is always still even though it shouldnt be, sitting at its base, always lit by moonlight, i have never seen it lit by the sun. Its a peaceful place. Its been awhile since i've gone there, so i can see why he took me there i needed to calm the fuck down and relax and this place washes it all away for a time. But even this place couldnt wash that sadness away. Where the fucking hell is it coming from?<br /> <br /> In my dreams i'm searching for something while running from something hunting me. I dont understand them. I need to start keeping a dream journal again.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any insights? (haha have at my crazyness!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:43:01-07:00","id":689321,"title":"","content":"man what is going on with my dreams!? EVERY time i fall asleep lately im stuck with super vivid realistic dreams its starting to piss me off as some of them turn into nightmares which wake me up. I'm not used to having frequent dreams like this. Yes i have vivid dreams when i do dream and remember it, but its not extremely often i remember them, but oooohhh not this week this week every fucking dream is pounding so hard into my brain ;&gt;&gt; <br /> <br /> Big old fuck you from my brain deciding I DONT EVER NEED SLEEP AGAIN!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}